{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The byte-cap and zero-parts fixes hold under static inspection, and the revised corruption tests retain the useful address/reason evidence without decoding bad bytes. The new `yin/def` path still appears unsound in two ways: it marks the binding before its operands run, and it assumes a variable named `yin/def` cannot have been shadowed in the module store."}}
